#!/bin/sh
# A source package carries src/seams. In a git checkout tools/vendor.sh
# makes it from SEAMS_CORE_SRC (or DSEAMS_ROOT), else from the revision
# pinned in tools/seams-core.ref, as for configure.
#
# chemfiles and readcon-core are optional. When either is found,
# READER_CPPFLAGS and READER_LIBS in src/Makevars.win name it. With
# neither, those variables stay empty and the build reads LAMMPS dumps
# and XYZ files.
if [ ! -f src/seams/seams_lang.cpp ] || [ ! -f inst/extdata/ice1h.lammpstrj ]; then
  if [ ! -f tools/vendor.sh ]; then
    echo "configure.win: src/seams is missing and there is no tools/vendor.sh to make it" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  sh tools/vendor.sh || exit 1
fi

: "${R_HOME:=$(R RHOME)}"
reader_eval=$(R_HOME="${R_HOME:-}" sh tools/find-readers.sh bundled) || exit 1
eval "$reader_eval"
READER_CPPFLAGS_VALUE=$dseams_reader_cppflags \
READER_LIBS_VALUE=$dseams_reader_libs \
awk '
  BEGIN {
    cpp = ENVIRON["READER_CPPFLAGS_VALUE"]
    libs = ENVIRON["READER_LIBS_VALUE"]
  }
  /^READER_CPPFLAGS=/ { print "READER_CPPFLAGS=" cpp; next }
  /^READER_LIBS=/ { print "READER_LIBS=" libs; next }
  { print }
' src/Makevars.win > src/Makevars.win.tmp
mv src/Makevars.win.tmp src/Makevars.win
echo "configure.win: $dseams_reader_message"
